Set Up Your Android Bash Terminal
-------------------------------------------------------------
To run the setup commands right on your phone without a laptop, you need a local command-line interface:
-------------------------------------------------------------
1. Download and open Termux (available via F-Droid or GitHub).
-------------------------------------------------------------
2. Give Termux access to your phone's internal storage folders by typing this command and hitting enter:
-------------------------------------------------------------
bash

termux-setup-storage

Use code with caution.
-------------------------------------------------------------
3. Update your core packages and install Node.js onto your phone's system partition:
-------------------------------------------------------------
bash 

pkg update && pkg install nodejs -y

Use code with caution.
-------------------------------------------------------------
4. Navigate directly into your application directory (replace the path with your actual folder location):
-------------------------------------------------------------
bash

cd /sdcard/Documents/FDARecalls

Use code with caution.
-------------------------------------------------------------
🚀 Step 3: Run the Native Packaging Commands
Now that your terminal is pointed at your code folder inside your phone, copy and paste these commands into Termux one line at a time to download the Capacitor wrapper engine:
-------------------------------------------------------------
bash

npm install @capacitor/core @capacitor/cli

Use code with caution.

(Downloads the framework container software onto your phone storage).
-------------------------------------------------------------
bash

npx cap init "FDA Recalls Tracker" "com.yourname.fdarecalls" --web-dir=.

Use code with caution.
-------------------------------------------------------------
(Initializes the structural layers).
-------------------------------------------------------------
bash

npm install @capacitor/android

npx cap add android

Use code with caution.
-------------------------------------------------------------
(Assembles the local native Android file architecture structures).
-------------------------------------------------------------
📦 Step 4: Compile into a Native App Without a PC
To convert those generated files into an installable .apk file directly on your ThinkPhone, you can install a mobile compiler system inside Termux:
-------------------------------------------------------------
1. Install the Android software development kit tools and a Java runtime package into your terminal shell environment:
-------------------------------------------------------------
bash

pkg install openjdk-17 android-tools -y

Use code with caution.
-------------------------------------------------------------
2. Sync your web changes directly into the native framework build configurations:
-------------------------------------------------------------
bash

npx cap copy android

Use code with caution.
-------------------------------------------------------------
3. Compile the production native build bundle:
-------------------------------------------------------------
bash

cd android && ./gradlew assembleDebug

Use code with caution.
-------------------------------------------------------------
Once the compilation script finishes running, your native installation packet will be generated at 

android/app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk.

 Open your phone's default Files app, locate that .apk file, and tap it to install your new self-updating tracker app.
-------------------------------------------------------------

